# ============================================================================
# Papyr backend build-context whitelist (legacy precedent).
#
# Strategy: exclude EVERYTHING, then allow back only what the image needs.
# Consequences:
#   * `.env*` files can never enter the build context (secrets rule);
#   * tests, caches, tooling config, git metadata never reach the builder;
#   * the image stays exactly app code + pinned requirements.
# The Dockerfile itself is always available to the builder even when
# excluded (BuildKit), so re-excluding it here is defense-in-depth.
# ============================================================================

# Exclude everything by default.
**

# Explicit allows — the only content the image needs.
!requirements.txt
!app/
!app/**

# Re-exclude anything the allows above would pull back in.
**/__pycache__/**
*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/**
.env
.env.*
Dockerfile*
compose.y*
*.md
.git
.github
.venv/
venv/
tests/
